# GenHealth assessment

- Follow [docs/SPEC.md](docs/SPEC.md), [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md), [docs/PROGRESS.md](docs/PROGRESS.md), [docs/PULL_REQUESTS.md](docs/PULL_REQUESTS.md).
- **Mandate:** update `docs/PULL_REQUESTS.md` when a PR starts or finishes. Skipping is a process failure.
- Work order: scaffold → CRUD → comments hygiene (PR2b) → UI+CORS → extract → confirm → deploy → README.
- **Comments:** follow `docs/COMMENTING.md` — concise why/constraint comments on non-obvious code in every PR; no noisy narration.
- Pause after each PR/checkpoint; do not start the next PR until the human says so.
- Ask when unclear; do not invent requirements. Log decisions in `docs/DECISIONS.md`.
- Prefer official docs (uv, FastAPI, Vite, Render, Gemini) over assumptions.
- MUST before SHOULD. S3 (rate limit/cache/batch/async) only after public deploy.
- Stuck >10m on SHOULD → Known issues + next MUST.
- No second scaffold, ORM, LLM client, or parallel app. Extend the monorepo.
- Extract returns drafts only; Orders persist only after confirm. UI confirms all saves/deletes.
- Security MVP: secrets in env; Gemini server-side; CORS allowlist; PDF-only + upload size limit; sanitize filenames; no secrets/stack in client errors; no PDF bytes in activity logs. Auth out of MVP.
- Demo data: Buffy names, fake only; any PDF accepted in MVP (not other MIME types).
- PRs: Summary, Test plan, Notes/risks (+ mirror in PULL_REQUESTS). Mid-checkpoint if approaching ~20 files.
